+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the same JSON Schema that it supplies to model providers, allowing malformed calls to be corrected through ordinary tool results.
+
+## Contract
+
+1. `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects missing required properties, incorrect declared types and invalid enum members before invoking an executor, returning a `ToolResponse` whose result names the property path and constraint without exposing input values; rejection logs likewise name paths and constraints without values, valid input including unknown properties reaches the executor unchanged exactly once without defaults or coercion, and an unknown tool still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects malformed calls privately and passes accepted input unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L25)).
+2. Static schemas compile at registration, with an uncompilable schema throwing an error naming its tool at registration, and successful compiled schemas are reused across ten executions without rereading the schema ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L70)).
+3. Function-valued definitions resolve for each execution and validate against the current schema object, including when switching back to a previously resolved object ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L99)).
+
+## Delivery obligations
+
+The execute method points here with a one-line doc comment; README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md describe validation, extra-property pass-through, rejection as a tool result and the existing five-round retry bound. The validator ships as a runtime dependency and the built package remains importable. Release documentation carries the executor migration note, a consumer-facing changelog and a minor version bump. A tool-loop regression demonstrates a rejected call followed by a corrected retry resolving processMessage with rejection text supplied to the next provider round.
